From 334b70ae491ac1137103ae22e8a82c854e3ecc88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:43:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(cli): turn the CLI into an HTTP client of the REST
 API

Every command used to open a fresh in-memory SQLiteRegistry, so nothing
it wrote survived the command: apply could only create (and dropped the
spec), get, describe and list never found anything, delete called the
physical delete and bypassed the controlled one, and --api-url was
parsed but never used. The package imported yaml and
forgemesh.controlplane without declaring either.

The commands now call /api/v1/inference-services with the standard
library's urllib, through the gateway by default (http://127.0.0.1:8081;
--api-url or FORGEMESH_API_URL reaches the control plane directly):

- apply GETs each document's service, POSTs it when it does not exist
  and otherwise PUTs it with the resourceVersion and uid just read,
  re-reading on 409 up to 5 times. It reports created, configured or
  unchanged, accepts multi-document YAML, JSON objects or arrays and
  stdin, and checks every document before sending anything.
- get and describe read one service; list follows nextPageToken and
  prints a table, a YAML stream or a JSON array.
- delete tells 204 (deleted) and 202 (Terminating) apart.
- wait polls until the service is Ready and the controller has observed
  the current generation, fails at once on Failed or Terminating, rides
  out 429 (honouring Retry-After), 502-504 and dropped connections, and
  gives up after --timeout; --for delete waits for the 404.

The API key comes from --api-key-file or FORGEMESH_API_KEY and is only
sent in the Authorization header; no message includes it, and redirects
are not followed, so it is never sent to another address. Error
envelopes and the gateway's plain-text 429 and 502 become messages with
the correlation id the CLI sends on every request, and the exit code
tells failure classes apart (usage 2, not found 3, conflict 4, rejected
5, auth 6, rate limited 7, server error 8, unavailable 9, no response
10, wait timeout 11, wait failed 12). A 404 that is not an API envelope
exits 1, so a wrong URL is not mistaken for a missing service.

Breaking: the output formats change, --tenant no longer defaults to
"default" and must match a document's tenantId instead of overriding
it, and failures no longer all exit 1. The old CLI kept nothing between
commands, so there is no data to migrate.

The package now declares only pyyaml, the one third-party distribution
it imports; it no longer depends on forgemesh-core and does not need the
control plane package. A packaging test compares the distributions the
CLI imports with the declared ones. The other unit tests run the
commands against a local HTTP server that mimics the API. The Makefile
comment that used the CLI as its --no-deps example now names
control-plane, which still depends on forgemesh-core.
